#X text 82 626 0: messages (see Messages below), f 64;
#X obj 60 670 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 694 0: signal left \; 1: signal right \; 2: events: value \, dump, f 64;
#X obj 60 770 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 794 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. mode 1 (see Settings below) \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices (master clock) \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly, f 64;
#X obj 60 1030 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1054 0 wav1 (127) Waveform of DCO1: 0 = square net (feet about \; 1:1:1:1) \, 127 = saw net (1:1/2:1/4:1/8 \, a step wave \, 16' +8 \; dB). Weights measured on a Poly-800\; continuous in between. \; 1 wav2 (127) Waveform of DCO2 \, same range. \; 2 har1 (64) Foot combination of DCO1. 15 original combinations \; at 0 \, 9 \, 18 ... 127 \, from one to the next a single foot fades \; in or out: 16' alone \, all feet at 64 \, 2' alone. \; 3 har2 (64) Foot combination of DCO2 \, same path. \; 4 intv (0) Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 \, 0-12 semitones. \; 5 detn (0) Detune of DCO2 downwards: the original's 4 steps 0 \, \; 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127. \; 6 lev1 (127) Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0) Level of DCO2 (DOUBLE only). Above full scale (lev1 \; + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 1306 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Settings\ (name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1330 mode (2) 1 = WHOLE: one DCO per voice \, 2 = DOUBLE: two DCOs \; oct1 \, oct2 (0) octave of DCO1 / DCO2 -1 \, 0 \, 1 \; nois (0) white noise level 0-15 \, sounds while a voice sounds \; sprd (0.5) stereo spread of the 4 voices 0-1 \; levl (0.5) output level 0-2 \; mrph (8) smoothing of wav \, har and lev changes in ms \; hold (1) released voices keep sounding until the next phrase \; a4 (440) tuning in Hz \; tune (0) master tune +-50 cents \; bnd (2) pitch bend range in semitones (original: up to 7) \; mgf (5) vibrato rate in Hz \; mgi (0) vibrato depth 0-160 cents (triangle on master clock) \; hsnp (1) plateau around each foot combination \, in har steps \; ch1 (0) MIDI channel for p v ch lists \, 0 = any \; tone (1) 1: output response measured on a Poly-800 with the \; VCF fully open (54 Hz high-pass \, 2 poles at 7.5 kHz) \, 0: off \; path (0) morph path of har: 0 = original (15 combinations) \, \; 1 = ring (8 combinations with 16' as root \, wraps 127 -> 0) \, \; 2 = figure eight (ring in the square net \, then in the saw net\; \; 16 points \, wraps\; wav is not used) \; norm (0) 0-1: hold the loudness constant over the morph \; pfad (1) 1: a fading foot rises in power \, not in amplitude \; pw1 \, pw2 (64) pulse width of DCO1 / DCO2: 0-127 = 3-97 % \, \; 64 = square\; works on every foot at once (see PWM) \; sync (0) 1: DCO2 restarts at every period of DCO1 (DOUBLE) \; swp2 (0) DCO2 pitch offset 0-48 semitones \, continuous \; fm (0) 0-127: FM index of DCO1 \, 0-8 (through zero above 45) \; fmr (1) FM ratio of the sine modulator to DCO1 \, 0.125-16 \; fms (0) FM source: 0 internal sine \, 1 DCO2 (cross FM) \; wsh1 \, wsh2 (0) Walsh loop position of DCO1 / DCO2 \, 0-127 \; wmx1 \, wmx2 (0) mix from the feet (0) to the Walsh loop (127) \; env1 \, env2 (0) DEG1 / DEG2 morph 0-127 (see Envelopes) \, \; -1 = own values a1 ... r2 \; leak (0) 1: released voices stay at -55 dB \, as on the original \; a1 d1 bp1 sl1 su1 r1 (0 0 31 0 31 0) DEG1 attack \, decay \, \; break point \, slope \, sustain \, release 0-31 (sets env1 to -1) \; a2 d2 bp2 sl2 su2 r2: the same for DEG2 \; port (0) portamento 0-127 = off to 3 s (not on the Poly-800) \; pmod (0) glide from: 0 the last note \, 1 the voice's own last \; note \, 2 the last note only while another key is held \; cut (99) VCF cutoff 0-99 (66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 4 poles \, measured) \; res (0) resonance 0-15 (no self-oscillation \, as the original) \; kbd (0) key tracking 0 off \, 1 half (ref C5) \, 2 full (ref C3) \; pol (2) DEG3 polarity 2 up \, 1 down\; egi (0) EG INT 0-15 \; trg (2) DEG3 trigger 1 single \, 2 multi \; env3 (0) DEG3 morph (VCF and noise) \, -1 = own a3 ... r3 \; a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3: DEG3 values 0-31, f 64;
#X obj 60 2110 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ the\ Poly-800\ makes\ its\ sound 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2134 One master clock feeds the MSM5232: 8 tone generators in two \; groups (TG0-3 = DCO1 \, TG4-7 = DCO2). Each key becomes an \; integer divider from the chip's ROM \, then a binary counter \; whose bits are the 16' \, 8' \, 4' and 2' squares \, locked in \; phase. The four feet of a group are summed to a square or a \; step saw. Tune \, bend and vibrato move the master clock \, so \; all voices move together. Detune thins out DCO2's clock. \; Every edge is band-limited: analog edges \, no aliasing., f 64;
#X obj 60 2290 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Foot\ path\ (har)\ -\ path\ 0 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2314 0: 16' / 9: 16'8' / 18: 16'8'4' / 27: 16'4' / 36: 16'4'2' \; 45: 16'2' / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: all feet / 73: 8'4'2' \; 82: 8'2' / 91: 8' / 100: 8'4' / 109: 4' / 118: 4'2' / 127: 2' \; On these values the sound is exactly the original. In \; between one foot fades \, so har can be modulated smoothly., f 64;
#X obj 60 2422 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Ring\ and\ figure\ eight\ -\ path\ 1\ and\ 2 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2446 path 1 \, root stays: 0: 16' / 16: 16'4' / 32: 16'4'2' / \; 48: 16'2' / 64: 16'8'2' / 79: all / 95: 16'8'4' / \; 111: 16'8' / 127: 16' again. wav sets the net. \; path 2 \, both nets: 0-56 the ring in the square net \, \; 64-119 in the saw net backwards \, 127: 16' square again. \; Both loops close \, so an LFO or ramp can turn endlessly. \; norm 1 keeps the level constant \, pfad 1 smooths the fades., f 64;
#X obj 60 2586 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PWM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2610 pw1 / pw2 turn every foot into a pulse: the AND of the foot \; with a copy shifted by part of its period \, so the falling \; edge stays on the counter step and the rising edge moves. \; On the saw net this gives pulse staircases. All edges stay \; band-limited\; norm also evens out the level of narrow pulses., f 64;
#X obj 60 2718 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Sync\ and\ FM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2742 sync 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every 16' period of DCO1 \, \; at the exact sub-sample time. Sweep DCO2 with swp2 (or intv \, \; oct2) for the classic sync sound\; lev1 0 to hear DCO2 alone. \; fm: linear FM of DCO1's counter rate by a sine at fmr times \; its 16' frequency (fms 0) or by DCO2 (fms 1). Above index 1 \; the counter runs backwards for a moment (through zero) \, so \; integer ratios stay harmonic. All edges stay band-limited., f 64;
#X obj 60 2882 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Walsh\ morph 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2906 The feet are Rademacher functions\; their products (XOR of \; the foot squares) are the 15 Walsh functions: two-level waves \; whose energy sits around harmonic 1 ... 8 of the 16'. wsh \; moves along a closed loop of them by sequency \, up through \; one of each pair and down through the other\; neighbours fade \; at equal power \, so the level stays. 0: 16' / 8: 8' / \; 17: 16'x4' / 25: 4' / 34: 16'x4'x2' / 42: 8'x2' / 51: 16'x2' / \; 59: 2' / 68: 16'x8'x2' / 76: 8'x4'x2' / 85: all / 93: 4'x2' / \; 102: 16'x8'x4' / 110: 8'x4' / 119: 16'x8' / 127 = 0. \; wmx fades from the feet sum to the Walsh loop., f 64;
#X obj 60 3094 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty VCF\ and\ DEG3 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3118 One 4-pole VCF for the instrument \, as the NJM2069 \, measured \; on a Poly-800: cutoff 0-99 = 66 Hz ... 20 kHz (13 steps per \; octave) \, resonance an uncompensated ladder (bass falls as it \; rises \, no self-oscillation). DEG3 (one \, paraphonic) moves the \; cutoff by up to 7.9 octaves (EG INT 15) and sets the noise \; level \, both linear in its level. Single trigger: only the \; first key starts DEG3\; multi: every key. Full tracking follows \; the highest key 1:1 (C3 nominal) \, half by 1/2 (C5 nominal)., f 64;
#X obj 60 3274 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Envelopes\ (DEG1\ /\ DEG2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3298 Each tone generator has its own 6-stage DEG as on the \; Poly-800 (attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release \; 0-31) \, measured on a real one: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, \; attack rises linearly (A31 about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and \; release fall at a constant dB per second (31: about 18 s \; to -40 dB). env1 / env2 morph through a loop of settings: \; 0 gate / 16 organ / 32 pluck / 48 piano / 64 long release / \; 79 pad / 95 swell / 111 brass / 127 = gate. A released voice \; releases at once\; hold 1 keeps it until the next phrase., f 64;
#X obj 60 3470 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ steps 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3494 Per-step values: connect the voice to [skpreset name] \; (outlet 2 -> inlet 0 \, outlet 0 -> voice inlet). A slot \; number 0-15 then recalls and keeps the values for a step. \; More in skpreset-help.pd (click to open)., f 64;
